  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Community Engagement in Papua New Guinea (BCEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Community Engagement in Papua New Guinea program seeks to support citizen-government engagement for improved service delivery and provision of public goods. The program works with a diverse portfolio of Papua New Guinean implementing partners from across government, civil society, church groups, and academia to deliver five distinct, but inter-related components, namely: Church Partnerships Program; Coalitions for Change; Media Development Initiative; Social Accountability; and Government of Papua New Guinea Partnerships. It has a particular emphasis on promoting inclusion and gender equality.</narrative>
  </description>
